Dear Verkada Hiring Team,

I am applying for the *Backend Engineer - Connectivity* position. I bring more than three years of professional software engineering experience, a recently completed Master of Science in Computer Science from Pace University, and production experience building Python APIs, distributed systems, Redis/PostgreSQL services, Kubernetes deployments, and high-reliability workflows. Verkada's mission to protect people and places through an integrated, cloud-based physical security platform makes this role especially meaningful to me.

At Sperse, I built a scalable distributed platform in Python, FastAPI, LangGraph, PostgreSQL, and Redis that routes high-concurrency requests across more than 40 specialized services for over 10,000 users. I designed clean REST APIs and a production MCP service exposing 160+ validated backend actions with structured schemas, monitoring, tenant-aware access control, and error isolation. I also developed durable microservice workflows with Temporal and Redis, adding retries, resumable execution, and live progress tracking for long-running jobs. This work maps directly to Verkada's need for low-latency, high-throughput, high-reliability architectures and scalable systems that interact with globally deployed products.

I have owned services through implementation, deployment, testing, and production operation. I deployed containerized workloads through Kubernetes, Docker, and GitHub Actions CI/CD, using OpenTelemetry trace-based evaluations to catch latency, accuracy, and safety regressions before release. Earlier at Qualitest, I designed and launched a cloud-agnostic Java and Spring Boot storage microservice backed by PostgreSQL and Redis, optimized data access with indexes and materialized views, and improved error recovery across more than 100,000 weekly AWS Step Functions executions.

I would welcome the opportunity to bring this backend engineering experience to Verkada's Connectivity team and help build reliable cloud services for hundreds of thousands of devices. I can be reached at #ph or #eml. Thank you for your time and consideration.

